i think that given the circumstances  the best way i can help now  is if i step aside and let government  get back  to governing and therefore that's what  i'll do  because i work for you  new york governor andrew cuomo resigned  after facing mounting investigations and  various claims of sexual harassment  in my mind i've never crossed  the line with anyone  but i didn't realize  the extent to which the line has been  redrawn his resignation came a week  after a state report concluded that he  had sexually harassed multiple women  and just days after one of those women  filed a criminal complaint  alleging he groped her at the executive  mansion last year the investigation  found that  governor andrew cuomo sexually harassed  current  and former new york state employees by  engaging in  unwelcome and non-consensual touching  and making numerous offensive comments  of a suggestive  and sexual nature that created a hostile  work  environment for women though he  ultimately stepped down  cuomo criticized the investigation as  being political and denied  all allegations of harassment i want you  to know directly from me  that i never touched anyone  inappropriately  or made inappropriate sexual advances  cuomo's resignation  ends a 10-year run as governor cutting  his third term short  and marring his political career in  controversy a career that began  four decades ago by his father's side a  man who has  taught us all very much in this room and  it was taught me  everything i know governor mario cuomo  and first lady michael  comey cuomo began building his political  reputation as an ambitious and hard  charging democrat  while working for his father governor  mario cuomo in the 1980s  in 1990 he married carrie kennedy  joining two powerful political families  in a union some called cuomo cuomo went  on to serve as president clinton's  housing secretary in the 90s before  making his first run for governor in  2002  but that year he bowed out of the race  before the democratic primary  with polls showing he had little chance  of winning shortly after  he and kennedy announced their divorce  in 2006  cuomo was elected new york attorney  general and in 2010  he announced another bid for governor we  must use this moment  to reorganize the government reform its  ethics  and restructure its finances he cruised  a victory as he denounced albany as a  cesspool  touted his record as a prosecutor and  proposed a fiscally moderate agenda  this state has no future if it is going  to be the tax capital of the nation  we have to send that signal this session  by passing a property tax cap  during his tenure cuomo tacked to the  left legalizing gay marriage  raising the minimum wage if you work  full time  you should be paid a wage that provides  a decent living  implementing strict gun control laws  today new york is proud  once again to pass a first in the nation  the red flag bill and championing big  infrastructure projects  despite his liberal policies he  maintained support from business leaders  and won re-election twice  in 2014 and 2018. then  as the early stages of the coronavirus  erupted in new york  he burst into the spotlight like never  before holding daily press briefings  that gained nationwide attention  if a person comes in and needs a  ventilator and you don't have a  ventilator the person  dies frankly there has been a laxness  on social distancing especially over  this past weekend  that is just wholly unacceptable the  federal government  cannot wipe their hands of this and say  oh the states  are responsible for testing i don't need  the president of the united states to  read the constitution for me  maybe he should have read the  constitution before he said  he had the power to open the states  cuomo's briefings made headlines  and earned him a speaking spot at the  democratic national convention  only a strong body can fight off the  virus  and america's divisions weakened it  donald trump didn't create the initial  division  the division created trump  he only made it worse he also  capitalized on the crisis  signing a 5.1 million dollar contract  for a book about his handling of the  pandemic  the book launched in october amid a rise  in coronavirus cases  then in december a former advisor  accused the governor of sexual  harassment on twitter  others began to follow charlotte bennett  a former assistant in cuomo's office  sat down with cbs evening news offering  details of her story  what were you thinking as he's asking  you  these questions i thought he's trying to  sleep with me  the governor is trying to sleep with me  and  i'm deeply uncomfortable  and i have to get out of this room as  soon as possible i've heard charlotte  and her lawyer and i understand what  they are saying  but they read into comments that i made  and draw inferences that i never meant  they ascribe motives i never had  and simply put they heard things  that i just didn't say in march cuomo  welcomed an independent investigation  but when the probe that he called for  ultimately detailed a pattern of  harassment  he called the report biased and  continued to deny all  allegations of misconduct trial by  newspaper  or biased reviews are not the way to  find the facts in this matter  meanwhile cuomo also faced probes  involving his handling of deaths at new  york nursing homes during the pandemic  in march of last year when new york  became the epicenter of the coronavirus  crisis  his administration mandated that nursing  homes accept patients with covid19 in a  bid to free up hospital beds  the policy was widely criticized for  accelerating deaths in nursing homes and  the state reversed the mandate  two months later cuomo defended the  policy  but his administration withheld  information about the number of nursing  home related deaths  cuomo said it was because the data  became political  it's not about pointing fingers or blame  it's that this became a political  football  right but even members of his own party  criticized the move  they just need to own up to some of the  mistakes that were made  the various investigations took their  toll on the governor  and political pressure mounted following  the release of the state's findings of  harassment  are you now calling on him to resign yes  facing criticism from the highest levels  of his own party as well as growing  momentum for impeachment  cuomo stepped down thank you  for the honor of serving you  it has been the honor of my lifetime  god bless you though cuomo is leaving  the governor's mansion  his troubles may not be over several  local prosecutor's offices  said they planned to look into the  conduct described in the report

